row 8,945-8,955 range for day. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0126 GMT [Dow Jones] KLCI +0.4% at 1465.68, tracking gains on Wall Street overnight; however, absence of fresh fundamental cues may keep key index confined to narrow band of 1460-1470 in subdued trading rest of day, dealer says, adding range-bound trading may persist in coming days. "Investors will stay generally cautious until the 2011 budget," dealer says. Government due to unveil 2011 budget on October 15. Among gainers, Gamuda (5398.KU) +1.6% at MYR3.86 after reporting 77% rise in FY10 earnings, Ingress (7122.KU) +2.4% at MYR0.845 after Thai unit gets contract to supply parts to Honda, Suzuki. Among decliners, AirAsia (5099.KU) down 1.4% at MYR2.11 on profit-taking after reaching record high earlier this week. (benjamin.low@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0119 GMT [Dow Jones] New Zealand's August trade data, particularly weaker-than-expected exports, reaffirms case RBNZ likely to remain on sidelines until global developments improve, says ANZ economist Mark Smith; "The weakening trend in commodity export prices suggest there could be more (export weakness) to come." Adds driving decrease in exports, down 11.5% on month, was a 10% fall in value of commodity-based exports with falls for meat, dairy, forestry; "Other exports held up reasonably well, increasing by 3.1% over the month." (lucy.craymer@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0117 GMT [Dow Jones] Singapore stocks rebound from yesterday's pullback, drawing strength from Wall Street's overnight gains. STI +0.3% at 3107.65, with resistance expected at year-to-date high of 3125. "There were no signs of quarterly window dressing as of yesterday, but we do not discount buying on dips and a bit more activity in the last two days of 3Q10," says CIMB. Gainers outnumbering decliners by almost 8 to 1 in broad market. Among blue chips, Wilmar (F34.SG) +1.3% at S$6.15, CityDev (C09.SG) +1.1% at S$12.52, \uc2 Singapore Press Holdings\uc2  (T39.SG) +1.0% at S$