sterday, \uc2 Sun Hung Kai Properties\uc2  (0016.HK) down 1.2% at HK$128.90, Henderson Land (0012.HK) down 2.0% at HK$53.75. (susanna.tai@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0045 GMT [Dow Jones] Australia's S&P/ASX 200 edges up 0.6% to 4695.5 after Tankan report and ahead of the China HSBC Manufacturing PMI at 0230 GMT, with IG Markets saying a stronger-than-expected reading from data for the world's second-largest economy likely to see mining stocks bid higher. Bellwethers BHP +1.1% and \uc2 Rio Tinto\uc2  +1.2% in morning trade. "Lower commodity prices yesterday prompted some profit taking but we're now seeing a bit of a scramble to put positions back on" says Peter Copeland, senior institutional trader at BBY. \uc2 Sigma Pharmaceuticals\uc2  flat after announcing 1H net loss of A$218.5 million. \uc2 Telstra\uc2  +1.5% after CEO \uc2 David Thodey\uc2  says company likely to reach agreement on NBN by Nov. 19. ASX shares -1% as CEO Robert Elstone says he still plans to step down around the time his contract expires in July next year. (andrew.critchlow@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0038 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/SGD hits new record low at 1.3162 overnight, bounces back in early Asian trade, last 1.3178 vs 1.3228 late Asia yesterday; trader at international bank says pair may rise above 1.3200 if MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "The tolerance band of MAS has shifted following gains in other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the basket which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tracks. The U.S. dollar is weakening but the MAS won't tolerate a very steep fall in the greenback," trader says; tips 1.3170-1.3230 range. (gaurav.raghuvanshi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0037 GMT [Dow Jones] China shares may consolidate but biased down as investors retreat to sidelines on widespread caution ahead of long holiday starting Friday. Shanghai Composite Index tipped to test support at 2600, after ending down 0.6% at 2611.35 yesterday. "The holiday factor dominates the market today and tomorrow, as investors are worried about Beijing coming out with policy shifts during the break, as well as movements in global markets while China is closed," says Li Xiaoxuan at Shenyin Wanguo Securities. Adds some profit taking expected ahead of holidays for stocks that have outperformed recently. Shenzhen index ends down 0.6% at 1163.32. (jean.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0035 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP tipped to move lower on broad USD weakness, overnight gains of U.S. equities. Pair may head towards 43.80 support from 44.10 late Tuesday; next resistance 44.30. "The peso should appreciate today, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to guard the 43.80 level," says local bank trader. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com) [ 09-28-10 2102ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100929e69t0000w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
