\par\par \b \uc2 POLL-JGB yields unlikely to rise as much as anticipated\b0\par\par\uc2 583 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2010\par 14:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * For poll data <BONDPOLL1>\par \par \uc2 * Forecasts for yields to rise cut on BOJ policy outlook\par \par \uc2 * 10-year yield seen at 1.30 percent in a year\par \par \uc2 By Shinichi Saoshiro\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Sept 28 (Reuters) - The prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  easing in Japan, as the country's economy struggles with deflation compounded by the rising yen, has reduced the scope for bond yields to gain over the next year from already low levels, a Reuters poll found.\par \par \uc2 In the quarterly poll, conducted by Reuters this week, the median forecast from 28 respondents for the benchmark 10-year JGB yield <JP10YTN=JBTC> at the end of December was 1.02 percent, below a forecast of 1.40 percent in the previous poll in June.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year JGB yield <JP10YTN=JBTC> stood at 0.955 percent on Tuesday, near a seven-year low of 0.895 percent in August, and is forecast to rise to just 1.30 percent over the coming year, down from a 12-month forecast of 1.50 percent in the prior poll.\par \par \uc2 "Yields are seen staying relatively low on the Bank of Japan continuing its easy monetary policy and the government sticking to its fiscal austerity stance," said Takehiro Sato, an economist at Morgan Stanley MUFG Securities.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are expected to continue extending the durations of their bond holdings under such circumstances."\par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley MUFG Securities forecasts the 10-year JGB yield at 1.00 percent a year from now, the low end of forecasts which range from 0.80 percent to 2.00 percent.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time in six years this month to stop the yen's advance to a 15-year high versus the dollar from damaging exports and fanning deflation.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan has so far left the yen it sold in the money market, adding to liquidity and fuelling expectations that it is prepared to keep conditions very easy.\par \par \uc2 It meets on Oct. 4-5 and expectations for more easing steps have increased as a result of the yen's rise. A boost in its bond-buying and expansion of a cheap fund-supply tool are seen as the most likely options.\par \par \uc2 The median forecast from 15 respondents for the two-year JGB yield <JP2YTN=JBTC> at the end of December was 0.13 percent, below the previous forecast of 0.20 percent.\par \par \uc2 The two-year yield was at 0.130 percent on Tuesday but hit 0.110 percent in August, its lowest in five years.\par \par \uc2 Helping soothe supply concerns, Japan is lining up an extra budget to stimulate the economy which some ministers say could be funded by tapping reserves rather than new bonds.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say though that the government still faces a tough task as it will have to balance the need to help a wobbly economy with its fiscal austerity stance when it compiles next year's budget.\par \par \uc2 Sato at Morgan Stanley MUFG Securities said yields could rise if the Japanese economy recovered faster than expected, but the downside risks appeared greater at this point.\par \par \uc2 (For an overview of the poll click on [US/INT])\par \par \uc2 (For money market and bond yield poll data <BONDPOLL1>)\par \par \uc2 (For a PDF summary, click on [BOND/PDF])\par \par \uc2 (Writing/reporting by Shinichi Saoshiro in Tokyo; polling by Bangalore Polling Unit; editing by Stephen Nisbet)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-BONDS-JAPAN/ POLL|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|J   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020101001e69s001dq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
