\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : New Euro Zone Downgrade Fears Knock Euro Lower\b0\par\par\uc2 By Nicholas Hastings   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 693 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 September 2010\par 11:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The euro came under a fresh wave of selling pressure Tuesday on renewed fears about euro zone downgrades.\par \par \uc2 At one stage the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell as far as $1.3381 but then bounced off support at that level. Analysts suggest that the euro could hit stop-losses and face a more violent fall if it breaks through the $1.3380 level.\par \par \uc2 See how the euro reacted to the downgrade fears:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4641"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.dowjoneswebservices.com/chart/view/4641}}}\par \par \uc2 The selloff came as the Spanish newspaper Expansion carried an article saying that analysts expect \uc2 Moody's\uc2  to reduce Spain's triple-A credit rating later this week. \uc2 Moody's\uc2  is the last of the major credit agencies to still have a top-grade rating for Spain.\par \par \uc2 Sentiment in the euro was knocked even further when a \uc2 Standard & Poor's\uc2  analyst told Irish radio that the credit rating for \uc2 Anglo Irish Bank\uc2  could be cut even lower if the bank needs more than a EUR35 billion recapitalization from the Irish government. S&P has already reduced the rating of the Irish bank by three notches.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was left mixed as the market continues to mull a report in the Wall Street Journal that the Fed is considering less aggressive quantitative easing this time around. In other words, it will only introduce more bond purchases gradually and as the market needs rather than announcing a large program as it did back in 2009.\par \par \uc2 Talk of increased QE is seen by some as a further negative for the dollar. Others argued, though, that a more gradual approach should be positive for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Or, as analysts at \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  said, such an exercise would be "less negative."\par \par \uc2 The market is now waiting to see if U.S. data later in the day, which are expected to show slightly lower house prices and a decline in consumer confidence, adds to pressure for more QE.\par \par \uc2 A series of Fed speakers both Tuesday and Wednesday could also provide further hints about what the Fed intends to do.\par \par \uc2 Fear of further Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the yen in a narrow trading range against the dollar, with the market now looking to see if the latest Bank of Japan Tankan survey early Wednesday increases pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen weak.\par \par \uc2 A disappointing Tankan would suggest that the Japanese economy is losing its competitive edge in export markets and needs to push the yen lower.\par \par \uc2 The pound initially came under pressure against the dollar despite an upbeat report from the International Monetary Fund, giving its wholesale support for the U.K. coalition government's deficit-slashing program. The IMF dismissed criticism that the spending cuts will lead to a double-dip recession.\par \par \uc2 However, sterling staged a bounce after the latest U.K. current account deficit narrowed unexpectedly in the second quarter due to a sharp increase in the income surplus. The deficit came in at GBP7.4 billion, down from revised GBP11.3 billion in the first three months of the year.\par \par \uc2 By midmorning, the euro has been knocked back to $1.3406 from $1.3444 late Monday in New York, according to EBS.\par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also down at Y112.92 from Y113.25, while the dollar was essentially flat at Y84.21 from Y84.25.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was nearly flat at CHF0.9862 compared with CHF0.9857, while the pound was down at $1.5821 from $1.5826 after falling as low as $1.5781.\par \par \uc2 By Nicholas Hastings, Dow Jones Newswires; 44 20 7842 9493; nick.hastings@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkBackEurope@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 28-09-10 0917GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1035 28038 4163 44462   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100928e69s000wd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
