\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Euro Needs More Good News - \uc2 Lloyds Banking Group\b0\par\par\uc2 1,200 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2010\par 10:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par Markettalk.eu@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0839 GMT [Dow Jones] After Friday's surge in risk appetite on better than expected German Ifo and U.S. durable goods the market will likely take a breather and consolidate this session says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lloyds Banking Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 . EUR/USD and EUR/JPY have already come under selling pressure in Tokyo Monday and the bank says with IMM data showing JPY long positions reduced after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and euro positions now moderately long, more evidence for euro strength will be needed to trigger another significant advance. EUR/USD trades at 1.3459, EUR/JPY at 113.33. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0838 GMT [Dow Jones] \uc2 Barclays Capital\uc2  suggests receive positions in back-end of India OIS curve as RBI may not hike rates much more while tight cash may support front-end. "We expect liquidity with banks and the government to turn negative in the first week of October and expect the repo rate to continue to be the operative rate, barring any liquidity injection measures by the RBI," says House. Suggests receive positions in 3-year to 5-year sector of OIS curve. Also recommends investors receive 2-year forward 1-year OIS, targeting 7.00%. Adds, OIS curve likely to move lower this week, tracking bond yields with 5-year OIS to move towards 6.95%. (nupur.acharya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0833 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PHP lower late, tracking broad USD weakness vs regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while equity fund inflows continue. Pair at 43.90 in heavy volume vs 44.09 late Friday. Pair may test 43.80 support Tuesday, though players expected to stay cautious due to chance of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says local bank trader; next resistance at 44.20. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0831 GMT [Dow Jones] SET Index expected to drift up further to 1050-1100 points by year-end, thanks largely to continuous portfolio inflows, says TISCO Securities' acting head of technical analysis Viwat Techapoonpol. SET last +1.1% at 962.26. Some THB30 billion to THB40 billion worth of offshore funds expected to continue flowing into Thai shares in October, November while around THB30 billion estimated to pour into Thai shares in 4Q via local long-term equity funds, or LTF. Thai individuals usually buy units of LTF just ahead of year-end to enjoy tax benefits. He notes that foreign investors unloaded some THB73 billion Thai shares during the peak of political unrest in April-May but only bought back around THB54 billion during June-September. Recommends bank stocks, energy plays. (phisanu.phromchanya@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0827 GMT [Dow Jones]--The ruble looks set to rebound against the US dollar, but buyers should wait until the greenback has stabilized before betting on the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says RBC. Additionally, the deadline for the payment of production and profit taxes should generate inflows in the early part of the week, it says. Ruble is trading at 35.34 against a basket of dollars and euros, stronger by 0.6%. (ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0823 GMT [Dow Jones] Gilts are up Monday, tracking bunds higher as investors look to pick up knocked-down safe-haven government bonds after the weak close Friday. A survey released overnight by Hometrack showed UK home prices fell again in September, adding to the recent run of weak data on the housing sector. There is no economic release of note Monday, although there are a clutch of releases in the US later this week and signs of weakness may support core government bonds, says \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . The final release of UK 2Q GDP and manufacturing PMI are also due this week. December gilts are up 0.37 at 123.78. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0822 GMT [Dow Jones] Soft U.S. data and dovish comments from the Fed's Bernanke Friday depress risk appetite and leave the EUR slipping at the start of the new week Monday. Trade tensions between China and the U.S. increase as the Beijing fails to accelerate the appreciation of the CNY. The EUR is down at $1.3451 while the USD is marginally lower at Y84.23, with investors remaining wary of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The GBP is down at $1.5806. (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0817 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/MYR falls to fresh 13-year low of 3.0885, vs 3.0920 late Friday; pair tracking broad USD weakness vs regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Stronger equity market (benchmark KLCI +1.1%), improved risk appetite, positive outlook for local economy also supporting MYR. "Unless there is a sudden change in sentiment, the dollar/ringgit is expected to continue its downtrend tomorrow," dealer says; pair tipped to test 3.0750 support near-term, though \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if pair falls sharply. Dealers say \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of buying at 3.0885 today. (benjamin.low@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0814 GMT [Dow Jones]--The ruble will be supported by end of the month corporate tax payment on Monday and Tuesday, as exporters sell dollars and euros and buy the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Unicredit\uc2  says. "The outflow of close to 300 billion rubles ($9.7 billion) in payments from the banking system will provide some support for the ruble via liquidity demand. It may also trigger sales of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by exporters." Ruble is trading at 35.34 against a basket of dollars and euros, stronger by 0.6%. (ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0808 GMT [Dow Jones] Little sign that China will bow to Washington's pressure and accelerate the CNY's advance. Beijing fixes the USD/CNY above 6.70 Monday. This, says \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 , is "leaving markets with the impression that it will continue appreciating its exchange rate only in small steps." The bank suggests this isn't surprising as "China has little other choice than to operate gradually on the exchange rate without risking the economy." (nick.hastings@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0802 GMT [Dow Jones] Earlier in the day USD/JPY matched Friday's post \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  low of 84.12 and now trades at 84.18. \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analyst Karen Jones says the rate is looking vulnerable and further slippage toward the 84.00-83.50 band should be allowed for. Topside, only above the 55 DMA at 85.57 will generate upside interest with a daily close above here opening risk toward 87.15 and 87.50. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0801 GMT [Dow Jones] The Hungarian forint is trading strongly against the euro, riding the wave of a Western European equity market rally and after a stronger-than-expected German Ifo index Friday. EUR/HUF is 277.0 from 277.36 Friday afternoon. Markets are eying Monday's rate setting meeting, where the Monetary Policy Council is seen leaving the key rate on hold at 5.25%, especially as the MPC pledged to hike rates to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in case of extreme weakening. Equilor expects EUR/HUF to drop to 272, if breaks a support around 277. (veronika.gulyas@dowjones.com) [ 09-27-10 0439ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100927e69r0005i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppi