\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro eases on profit-taking; dollar flat vs yen\b0\par\par\uc2 743 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2010\par 02:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Euro down 0.2 pct at $1.3461 <EUR=> after 5-month high\par \par \uc2 * Fed easing expectations keep dollar under pressure\par \par \uc2 * CFTC data shows shift to euro longs\par \par \uc2 * Euro near-term key tech level around $1.3510\par \par \uc2 (Releads, adds quotes, changes dateline prvs TOKYO)\par \par \uc2 By Tamawa Desai\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 27 (Reuters) - The euro took a breather on Monday after hitting five-month highs against the dollar late last week but losses were limited as the greenback remained under pressure on expectations of more U.S. monetary easing.\par \par \uc2 The dollar steadied against the yen above 84 yen as selling by Japanese exporters and institutional investors ahead of the fiscal half-year end was offset by wariness of more yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Traders said the euro was facing some profit-taking against the dollar after gaining 6 percent on the dollar this month and hitting its highest since April on Friday at $1.3496 <EUR=> but traders saw potential for further gains. At 0732 GMT, the euro was down 0.2 percent at $1.3461 <EUR=>.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve last week signalled it could loosen monetary policy further to support a sluggish economy.\par \par \uc2 "The euro is not being bought on its own merits, and the market will continue to sell dollars into the (Fed's) November meeting on expectations of more easing," said Lee Hardman, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at \uc2 Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi\uc2  UFJ. "That will also continue to support equities and commodity prices."\par \par \uc2 Latest data from the Commodity Futures Trading Commission showed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators moved to a net long position in the euro for the first time this year. [IMM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 ]\par \par \uc2 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Graphic on latest \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  positioning {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://r.reuters.com/kus26k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://r.reuters.com/kus26k}}}\uc2  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 "The euro has been surprisingly resilient to renewed sovereign debt concerns and similarly we don't expect softer data to much damage to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week," analysts at Credit Agricole CIB said in a note.\par \par \uc2 The euro's next key level stood at $1.3510, a 50 percent retracement of its fall from above $1.51 last November to its June low below $1.19. There was also talk of a barrier at $1.3525 with stop-loss buy orders above that level.\par \par \uc2 The market will watch European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tenders due to expire this week, with banks preparing to repay 225 billion euros of 12-, six- and three-month funds to the ECB on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Some say it may make traders cautious on the euro, while others say a withdrawal of funds from the banking system will boost lending rates and provide support for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The dollar index <=USD><.DXY>, a measure of its performance against six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was little changed at 79.35 after dropping to its lowest in almost eight months on Friday at 79.25. It fell through the 61.8 percent retracement of its rally from November to June on Friday, a bearish signal.\par \par \uc2 WARY TO CHASE YEN\par \par \uc2 The dollar held steady at 84.14 yen <JPY=>, near Friday's low of 84.12 and more than a yen above the 15-year low of 82.87 hit shortly before Japanese authorities acted nearly two weeks ago to sell yen for the first time in six years.\par \par \uc2 "Since this is the week when the fiscal half-year comes to an end, I think there will be a decent amount of (dollar) selling," said a senior trader at a major Japanese bank. "But because we are in such a situation, that also means that wariness toward \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is strong."\par \par \uc2 He doubted the dollar would fall rapidly even if stop-loss sell orders near 84.00 yen were triggered, adding, "It's scary to sell the downside."\par \par \uc2 The dollar spiked against the yen on rumours of further yen-selling action on Friday but Prime Minister Naoto Kan said he was unaware of any new market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . [ID:nN24270952]\par \par \uc2 Some traders said the dollar came off its initial weakness after Chinese authorities lowered its mid-point on the yuan after nine days of higher yuan fixings. [ID:nTOE68Q034]\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar hit a two-year high of $0.9623 before last trading at $0.9599, up 0.1 percent <AUD=D4>.\par \par \uc2 (Graphics by Scott Barber, additional reporting by Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  team)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 3)|LANGEN|C|D|E|M|O|U|MTL|GRO|SOF|OIL|J|RBN|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100927e69r00017\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
