\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 27\b0\par\par\uc2 2,166 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2010\par 09:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =JAPAN ECON MIN: GOVT SHOULD CONSIDER ADDITIONAL BONDS FOR EXTRA BUDGET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government should not rule out issuing additional government bonds to help finance an extra budget because such debt would be temporary in nature and therefore not run counter to the long-term goal of improving fiscal health, Minister of State for Economic and Fiscal Policy Banri Kaieda said Monday. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  =UPDATE: JAPAN EXPORT GROWTH SLOWS AS STRONG YEN WEIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese export growth slowed in August due to the strong yen and slack buying overseas, stoking concerns that the country's export-driven economy may lose more steam ahead. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA TARGETS LAND HOARDING, PUSHES PUBLIC HOUSING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China said Monday companies that haven't started developing land more than a year after acquiring a site at auction are banned from making bids in other auctions, in its latest effort to stabilize the housing market. (published 0432 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EX-MOF SHINOHARA: 'DANGEROUS' TO LINK \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , CHINA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't undermine multilateral efforts to get China to boost the yuan's value, a former top Japanese official said Monday. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EX-PBOC ADVISER: CHINA TO KEEP DIVERSIFYING RESERVES; YUAN TO RISE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China will continue to shift its foreign reserves into non-dollar assets, but U.S. government debt will remain the prime holding, former \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  adviser Fan Gang said Monday. (published 0652 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: THAILAND REVISES UP 2010 GDP GROWTH FORECAST TO 7.5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday revised up its economic growth forecast for 2010 to 7.5%, from 5.5% projected three months earlier, due mainly to the robust economic momentum in the first half and continuous strong performance of the export sector. (published 0613 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: MALAYSIA 2ND FINANCE MINISTER: 2010 GROWTH MAY TOP 7% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's economic growth rate may exceed 7% this year if global economic conditions aren't as bad as originally feared, Second Finance Minister Ahmad Husni Hanadzlah said Monday. (published 0637 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA MINING TAX POLICY TRANSITION GROUP WORK TO CONCLUDE END 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian government on Monday said it intends to wrap up its consultation process on a planned new mining tax by the end of the year and will release an issues paper by month's end. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: INDONESIA PARLIAMENT OPPOSES 15% POWER TARIFF HIKE NEXT YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An Indonesian parliamentary commission has turned down a plan by the government to raise electricity tariffs by an average of 15% next year, a lawmaker said Monday. (published 0416 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SRI LANKA SEEKS TO PRICE 10-YEAR DOLLAR BOND TO YIELD 6.5% -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government of Sri Lanka hopes to price a benchmark-sized dollar bond as early as today, a person close to the deal said Monday. (published 0304 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILIPPINE TREASURY PLANS PHP75 BLN DOMESTIC BORROWING IN 4Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine treasury plans to offer during auctions scheduled in the fourth quarter a total of PHP75 billion of paper, down by around a third of the average volume issued in each of the first three quarters of 2010, according to a borrowing schedule it released Monday. (published 0302 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KOREA ELECTRIC TO PRICE BENCHMARK 5-YEAR DOLLAR BONDS MONDAY - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Electric Power Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to issue U.S. dollar-denominated benchmark bonds with a five-year maturity and will price them today, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Monday. (published 0418 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =FOCUS: INDIA SWAPS MAY RALLY MORE ON RATE HIKES, TIGHT CASH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indian interest-rate swaps may be primed for further gains, especially in the short end, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  seems set to tighten monetary policy more than the market has priced in. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UNILEVER TO ACQUIRE ALBERTO CULVER FOR $3.7 BILLION IN CASH >UL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Unilever PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  (UL, ULVR.LN), the Anglo-Dutch consumer products giant, said Monday that it has entered into a definitive agreement to acquire \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alberto Culver Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (ACV, ACVA), maker of the Alberto VO5 hair-care products, for $3.7 billion in cash. (Published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AIA GROUP WON'T BE SELLING NEW SHARES IN HK IPO - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 AIA Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the pan-Asian life unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 American International Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., won't be selling new shares in its planned Hong Kong initial public offering, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Monday. (published 0157 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 HYUNDAI MOTOR\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO SUBMIT LETTER OF INTENT FOR HYUNDAI ENGINEERING MONDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., South Korea's No. 1 auto maker by sales, said it will submit a letter of intent to acquire a controlling stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Engineering & Construction Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to the construction firm's creditors on Monday in a bid to diversify its business portfolio. (published 0623 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par HENDERSON LAND: VICE CHAIRMAN STUDYING POSSIBILITY OF BUYING TVB STAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Henderson Land Development Ltd. said Monday its vice chairman, Peter Lee, is studying the possibility of buying a stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Television Broadcasts Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and is in contact with the local broadcaster's controlling shareholder, Shaw Brothers Ltd. (published 0548 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par COAL INDIA IPO LIKELY TO BE PRICED AROUND INR250/SHARE - SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 Coal India Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s initial public offering is likely to be priced around INR250 a share, two people with direct knowledge of the matter said Monday. (published 0350 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA SUNTIEN TO RAISE UP TO US$369.1 MLN IN HK IPO - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Suntien Green Energy Corp. aims to raise up to US$369.1 million from an initial public offering ahead of a listing in Hong Kong on Oct. 13, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Monday. (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TVB: HALTED SHARES TO LOOK INTO TRADING VOLATILITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Broadcaster Television Broadcasts Ltd. said Monday it halted its shares minutes before the opening bell to look into the "very volatile" pre-market trading of its shares, with the stock up nearly 17%. (published 0247 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WESFARMERS TO INVEST A$600M IN BUNNINGS HARDWARE CHAIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wesfarmers Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on Monday said it will invest over A$600 million in its Bunnings hardware store chain in New South Wales state. (published 2257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NINGBO PORT: TO LIST IN SHANGHAI TUESDAY AFTER IPO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ningbo Port Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a major port operator in eastern China, said it plans to list its shares on the Shanghai Stock Exchange Tuesday after it raised CNY7.4 billion from its initial public offering. (published 0012 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DBS INVESTS S$200M IN TECHNOLOGY, SUPPORT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN SINGAPORE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 DBS Group Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Monday it has invested S$200 million in the bank's new facility called the DBS Asia Hub, which will accommodate most of the bank's technology, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and support functions. (published 0257 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOWER BERSAMA SETS INDICATIVE OFFERING PRICE AT IDR1,600-IDR2,100/SHARE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Tower Bersama Infrastructure has set an indicative offering price of between IDR1,6100 and IDR2,100 per share for its plan to sell a 15.86% stake, or 755 million shares, through an initial public offering between Oct. 18 and Oct. 20, Tower President Director Herman Setiabudi told reporters Monday. (published 0453 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NUFARM GETS COVENANT WAIVERS, FUNDING FACILITY TO MID-DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nufarm Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it has agreed a waiver on its banking covenants and secured funding through to the middle of December, but will suspend any full-year dividend as it struggles to escape a debt pile estimated at A$620 million. (published 0131 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NINE DRAGONS PAPER LAST FY NET PROFIT UP 30% AT CNY2.17 BLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nine Dragons Paper Ltd. said Monday its net profit for the 12 months ended June 30 rose 30%, helped by a rebound in product prices and stronger demand amid the global economic recovery. (published 0614 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BARITO PACIFIC: TO MERGE TRI POLYTA AND CHANDRA ASRI \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT Barito Pacific\f28 \uc2 \f2  will merge its two units to create one of the largest integrated petrochemical companies in Asia in term of production capacity and assets, the company said Monday. (published 0130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =ONE97 COMMUNICATIONS CHAIRMAN: EXPECT TO LIST FIRM BY DECEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mobile phone software company \f28 \uc2 \f2 One97 Communications Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . expects approval from India's capital markets regulator for its INR1.20 billion initial public offering "anytime" and is looking to list its shares on the bourses by December, its chairman said. (published 0551 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TAIWAN GOVERNMENT: ELPIDA PLANS TO SET UP RESEARCH CENTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese memory-chip maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Elpida Memory Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to set up a center for research and development in Taiwan, an official at Taiwan's Ministry of Economic Affairs said Monday. (published 0147 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PHILEX MINING TRANSFERS ALL ENERGY ASSETS TO UNIT PHILEX PETROLEUM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Philex Mining Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the Philippines' most profitable gold and copper miner, said Monday that it will transfer all its energy assets, including a stake in an oil and gas exploration company in the U.K., to its wholly-owned unit Philex Petroleum Corp. (published 0142 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES HIGHER; EXPORTERS LEAD TOKYO MARKET UP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian shares rose Monday as investors took heart from Wall Street's strong performance on Friday, with export stocks leading the Tokyo market higher. (Published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA MINING TAX POLICY TRANSITION GROUP WORK TO CONCLUDE END 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian government on Monday said it intends to wrap up its consultation process on a planned new mining tax by the end of the year and will release an issues paper by month's end. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par METGASCO: FLOATING LNG, GLADSTONE PLANT AMONG OPTIONS FOR GAS DEVELOPMENT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 27-09-10 0717GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Metgasco Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday it is considering a floating LNG vessel offshore Australia's New South Wales state among other options for developing its gas reserves in the state. (published 2321 GMT Sunday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KUWAIT OIL MINISTER: EXPECT NO CHANGE IN OPEC QUOTA AT NEXT MEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Organization Of Petroleum Exporting Countries is unlikely to change production quotas at its next meeting in Vienna, scheduled for Oct. 14, as current oil prices are "comfortable," Kuwait's Oil Minister said Monday. (published 0537 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA PM OUTLINES NEW CARBON COMMITTEE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Prime Minister Julia Gillard on Monday outlined details of a new multi-party committee on climate change as her Labor party reiterated plans to introduce a carbon pricing mechanism. (published 0616 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: RUSSIA SECHIN: EXPECTS CHINA GAS SUPPLY DEAL IN 1H 2011 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An agreement for Russia to supply natural gas to China, which has been under negotiation for four years, is expected to be signed in the first half of 2011, Igor Sechin, Russian Deputy Prime Minister said Monday. (published 0353 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: XSTRATA, TOHOKU ELECTRIC AGREE TO OCT-SEP TERM COAL PRICE AT $97.70/TON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Xstrata PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  (XTA.LN) has agreed to sell around 1.2 million metric tons of Australian thermal coal to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tohoku Electric Power Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (9506.TO) for the October-September period at $97.70 a metric ton, a person familiar with the deal said Monday.(published 0223 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: OIL DATA: JAPAN ENERGY DEMAND UP ON AUGUST HEAT; COOLING NOW \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's energy imports rose across the board in August, with the on-year rise unlikely to be sustained in September, as the summer's extraordinarily hot weather didn't carry over into the autumn. (published 0450 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CNPC: RUSSIA-CHINA CRUDE OIL PIPELINE OFFICIALLY \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONAL\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  NOV 1 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The first crude oil pipeline between Russia and China will be \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officially on November 1, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jiang Jiemin\f28 \uc2 \f2 , President of \f28 \uc2 \f2 China National Petroleum Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA HUADIAN CORP IN RUSSIA POWER PLANT JOINT VENTURE -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Huadian Corp., one of China's five major power utilities, is expected later Monday to sign an agreement with a Russian company to build a 480-megawatts power station in Russia, a person close to the agreement said. (published 0436 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: INDONESIA PARLIAMENT OPPOSES 15% POWER TARIFF HIKE NEXT YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An Indonesian parliamentary commission has turned down a plan by the government to raise electricity tariffs by an average of 15% next year, a lawmaker said Monday. (published 0416 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KOGAS\f28 \uc2 \f2  SIGNS DEAL TO IMPORT 2.5 MLN TONS OF LNG FROM \f28 \uc2 \f2 GDF SUEZ\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Gas Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., South Korea's largest liquefied natural gas supplier, said Monday that it has signed a deal to import a total of 2.5 million tons of liquefied natural gas from French utility \f28 \uc2 \f2 GDF Suez SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  . (published 0140 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ZIJIN MINING: UNIT'S TIN MINE SUSPENDED PRODUCTION DUE TO TYPHOON \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Zijin Mining Group Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Sunday that a tin mine in Guangdong province owned by its unit Xinyi Zijin Mining Company Ltd. has suspended production after electricity and other services were cut at the mine in the aftermath of Typhoon Fanapi. (published 0221 GMT) [ 27-09-10 0717GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100927e69r000g2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
