\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 845 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2010\par 07:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN EXPORT GROWTH SLOWS AS STRONG YEN WEIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese export growth slowed in August due to the strong yen and slack buying overseas, stoking concerns that the country's export-driven economy may lose more steam ahead. (published 0235 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA TARGETS LAND HOARDING, PUSHES PUBLIC HOUSING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China said Monday companies that haven't started developing land more than a year after acquiring a site at auction are banned from making bids in other auctions, in its latest effort to stabilize the housing market. (published 0432 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ EYES ADDITIONAL EASING STEPS AT OCT MEETING - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan is moving in the direction of introducing additional monetary easing steps at one of its upcoming policy board meetings in October, the Mainichi Shimbun reported over the weekend. (published 2252 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EX-MOF SHINOHARA: 'DANGEROUS' TO LINK \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , CHINA \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't undermine multilateral efforts to get China to boost the yuan's value, a former top Japanese official said Monday. (published 0226 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par IMF SHINOHARA PRAISES MALAYSIA FOR MULLING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  LIBERALIZATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A top International Monetary Fund official Monday praised Malaysia for considering measures to liberalize trade in the ringgit. (published 0241 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MALAYSIA 2ND FINANCE MINISTER: 2010 GDP GROWTH LIKELY 6.0% TO 7.0% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's economy is likely to grow between 6.0% and 7.0% this year, Second Finance Minister Ahmad Husni Hanadzlah said Monday. (published 0409 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI FINANCE MINISTRY UPS 2010 GDP GROWTH FORECAST TO 7.5% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Monday revised up its economic growth forecast for 2010 to 7.5%, from 5.5% projected three months earlier, due mainly to the robust economic momentum in the first half and continuous strong performance in the export sector. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par VIETNAM JANUARY-SEPTEMBER GDP UP 6.52% ON YEAR - REPORT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's gross domestic product in the first nine months of this year grew 6.52% from a year earlier, state media said Monday, citing a statement from the Ministry of Planning and Investment. (published 0223 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA MINING TAX POLICY TRANSITION GROUP WORK TO CONCLUDE END 2010 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Australian government on Monday said it intends to wrap up its consultation process on a planned new mining tax by the end of the year and will release an issues paper by month's end. (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: UK SEPTEMBER HOUSE PRICES -0.4%MM, +1.0%YY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. house prices fell for a third straight month in September and by the biggest margin since March 2009 as consumer caution weighs on demand for property, which also declined for a third consecutive month, a survey shows Monday. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: INDONESIA PARLIAMENT OPPOSES 15% POWER TARIFF HIKE NEXT YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An Indonesian parliamentary commission has turned down a plan by the government to raise electricity tariffs by an average of 15% next year, a lawmaker said Monday. (published 0416 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par THAI FIN MIN: CAN'T SAY POLITICAL UNREST 'GONE FOR GOOD' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai Finance Minister Korn Chatikavanji Monday said his government has probably not seen the end of the recent political unrest. (published 0413 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SRI LANKA SEEKS TO PRICE 10-YEAR DOLLAR BOND TO YIELD 6.5% -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government of Sri Lanka hopes to price a benchmark-sized dollar bond as early as today, a person close to the deal said Monday. (published 0304 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINE TREASURY PLANS PHP75 BLN DOMESTIC BORROWING IN 4Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine treasury plans to offer during auctions scheduled in the fourth quarter a total of PHP75 billion of paper, down by around a third of the average volume issued in each of the first three quarters of 2010, according to a borrowing schedule it released Monday. (published 0302 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA ELECTRIC TO PRICE BENCHMARK 5-YEAR DOLLAR BONDS MONDAY - TERM SHEET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea Electric Power Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to issue U.S. dollar-denominated benchmark bonds with a five-year maturity and will price them today, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires Monday. (published 0418 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par   ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: DOLLAR/YEN OPTIONS RISE AFTER QUIET WEEK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen options rose slightly in Tokyo Monday as players returned to the market following a relatively quiet week marked by two national holidays. (published 0310 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =US MONEY WEEK AHEAD: TREASURY AUCTIONS TO BENEFIT FROM FED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After a two-week hiatus, the Treasury market faces another round of auctions next week that should draw strong demand from investors on elevated expectations the Federal Reserve will launch another large-scale bond-buying program. (published 2200 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =HEARD ON THE STREET: TALK IS CHEAP FOR FANNIE AND FREDDIE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 When it comes to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fannie Mae\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Freddie Mac\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the most likely course of action over the coming year might end up being inaction. Not that you would know, listening to the Obama administration or its Republican opponents. Both are preparing plans to overhaul the mortgage giants and housing finance. (published 2124 GMT) [ 27-09-10 0502GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100927e69r000au\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
