\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,178 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2010\par 10:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: EURO-ZONE ECONOMIC RECOVERY SLACKENED IN SEP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The euro-zone economy continued to lose momentum in September, data from the Centre for Economic Policy Research and the Bank of Italy showed Friday. (published 0730 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TSE PRESIDENT ENCOURAGES GOVERNMENT ACTION AS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GOES UNCONFIRMED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The president of the Tokyo Stock Exchange Friday encouraged the government to continue taking action against the strong yen, amid speculation the Japanese authorities were responsible for the U.S. dollar's jump against the yen during afternoon trade. (published 0720 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  SENIOR VICE FINANCE MINISTER: HAVEN'T HEARD ABOUT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Senior Vice Finance Minister Fumihiko Igarashi told Dow Jones Newswires Friday he had neither heard about any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market during the day, nor had he discussed \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy with Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda. (published 0720 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER NODA: NO COMMENT ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Minister of Finance Yoshihiko Noda declined to comment on whether the government had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday after the U.S. dollar jumped against the yen. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CONDUCTS YEN-SELLING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : MARKET SOURCE -KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government and the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appear to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets by selling yen Friday afternoon, Kyodo News reported, quoting market sources. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN ECONOMY MINISTER SAYS CHINA SPAT POSES ECONOMIC RISKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said Friday that growing diplomatic tensions with China pose risks to the Japanese economy, highlighting Tokyo's concern that a territorial dispute with its Asian neighbor could become an economic headache. (published 0338 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER AGAIN WARNS OF DECISIVE YEN STEPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister said Friday the government will take "decisive" measures in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if necessary, reminding market participants that Tokyo may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again to weaken the yen should they push it up too much too quickly. (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: FRENCH 2Q FINAL GDP BETTER THAN INITIAL ESTIMATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The French economy grew faster than initially estimated in the second quarter, supported by consumer spending and gross fixed capital formation, according to official data released Friday. (published 0538 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PM KAN SUGGESTS FINANCING EXTRA BUDGET WITHOUT BOND ISSUANCE -KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan suggested that the government would not issue any new bonds to finance an extra budget for the current fiscal year, which could include emergency outlays for additional stimulus measures, Kyodo News reported Friday. (published 0139 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA POSTS NARROWER DEFICIT, PLEDGES FISCAL DISCIPLINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Labor government on Friday renewed its commitment to strict fiscal discipline to restore the budget to surplus by the year starting July 1, 2012, after unveiling a narrower-than-expected deficit for the last financial year. (published 0133 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S TREASURY EXPECTS ECON TO RETURN TO FULL CAPACITY; INFLATION RISK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A bustling Australian economy will require policy makers to pull on both the fiscal and monetary levers in the second term of the recently elected minority Labor government, as a mining boom stokes the bellows of inflation, Australia's Treasury Department said Friday. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ: GOV SHIRAKAWA SAYS NO PLAN TO RESIGN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan on Friday denied market rumors of Gov. Masaaki Shirakawa's possible departure, quoting him as saying he has "no plan" to step down. (published 0609 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK OF RUSSIA DEFENDED RUBLE AMID CURRENT ACCOUNT WEAKNESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold $600 million from its reserves in September to defend the ruble, which was weakening as the country's current-account balance deteriorated, Chairman Sergei Ignatyev said Friday. (published 0757 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: SINGAPORE AUGUST MANUFACTURING OUTPUT UP 8.1% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's manufacturing output grew a less-than-expected 8.1% from a year earlier in August due to a drop in the volatile pharmaceuticals sector. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par DATA SNAP: VIETNAM SEPTEMBER CPI UP 8.92% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's consumer price index rose 8.92% in September from a year earlier, led by higher prices of housing and building materials, food and education services, the General Statistics Office said Friday. (published 0428 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK OF KOREA TO MAINTAIN SOFT LOAN CEILING AT KRW8.5T IN 4Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea will leave the ceiling on its soft loans to commercial banks unchanged at KRW8.5 trillion in the last quarter of the year, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a statement Friday. (published 0301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS: EURO BULLS MUST HAVE HAD ENOUGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Frustration equals being a euro bull. Earlier this week, everything was falling into place for another euro rally against the dollar. The U.S. Federal Reserve admitted, much to the surprise of many, that quantitative easing is still very much a monetary option. (published 0715 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN INTEREST RATE TECHNICALS: BONDS REMAIN STRONG \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday BUND: Bulls remain in control of the near-term after keeping the upside gap at 130.25 intact, and resistance at 131.58 is insecure. A break above 131.58 would create room for further gains towards 131.68, and 132.20 on concerted strength. There is risk of downside consolidation towards 130.70, but only below 130.47 would concern bulls. Weekly chart BUND trend: Bearish. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par EUROPEAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TECHNICALS: GBP GATHERING SOME STRENGTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Intraday EUR/USD: Bulls will look to extend the recovery off Thursday's low at 1.3286 by forcing a break above resistance at 1.3356. The 1.3286 level would become a near-term bear failure on a break above 1.3356, creating room for further gains to the 1.3415 lower high, and leaving Wednesday's peak at 1.3441 vulnerable. Only a break below 1.3286 would put bears in control of the near-term, exposing 1.3160 and 1.3100. Weekly chart EUR/USD trend: Bullish. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: FOOD INFLATION UNLIKELY TO BOOST ASIAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 A spike in food prices may boost overall inflation in Asia, but likely not by enough to seriously accelerate the rise in the region's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0449 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FOCUS: CHINA SHIFTS PROPERTY MKT FOCUS, TO BOOST CHEAP HOUSING SUPPLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Seeking to stabilize property prices without harming its economy, China is moving toward a strategy of building more public housing rather than tightening the private segment of the market. (published 0452 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FOCUS: CANADIAN BANKS TO TEST COVERED BONDS DOWN UNDER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canadian covered-bond issuers are testing a new route to Asia -- through Australia -- that could provide an opening for the covered-bond market to expand beyond its core base in Europe. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MONEY TALKS: PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO HUNKER DOWN FOR LONGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is in no hurry to raise interest rates. (published 0125 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VIEW: YEN GAINS PROMPT WATCH FOR SIGNS OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell Thursday to its lowest level in more than a week versus the yen, leaving traders on watch for signs of fresh Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 2024 GMT) [ 24-09-10 0801GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100924e69o000in\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
