\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 24\b0\par\par\uc2 1,777 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 September 2010\par 09:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FINANCE MINISTER NODA: NO COMMENT ON \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Minister of Finance Yoshihiko Noda declined to comment on whether the government had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market Friday after the U.S. dollar jumped against the yen. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  CONDUCTS YEN-SELLING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : MARKET SOURCE -KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese government and the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appear to have \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets by selling yen Friday afternoon, Kyodo News reported, quoting market sources. (published 0438 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =WSJ: JAPAN PROSECUTORS TO RELEASE CHINESE BOAT CAPTAIN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan prosecutors Friday announced their decision to release a Chinese sea captain involved in a ship collision in the East China Sea early this month, amid escalating tension between the two nations. (published 0652 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: JAPAN FINANCE MINISTER AGAIN WARNS OF DECISIVE YEN STEPS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister said Friday the government will take "decisive" measures in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if necessary, reminding market participants that Tokyo may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again to weaken the yen should they push it up too much too quickly. (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN PM KAN SUGGESTS FINANCING EXTRA BUDGET WITHOUT BOND ISSUANCE -KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan suggested that the government would not issue any new bonds to finance an extra budget for the current fiscal year, which could include emergency outlays for additional stimulus measures, Kyodo News reported Friday. (published 0139 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA POSTS NARROWER DEFICIT, PLEDGES FISCAL DISCIPLINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Labor government on Friday renewed its commitment to strict fiscal discipline to restore the budget to surplus by the year starting July 1, 2012, after unveiling a narrower-than-expected deficit for the last financial year. (published 0133 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S TREASURY EXPECTS ECONOMY TO RETURN TO FULL CAPACITY; INFLATION RISK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A bustling Australian economy will require policy makers to pull on both the fiscal and monetary levers in the second term of the recently elected minority Labor government, as a mining boom stokes the bellows of inflation, Australia's Treasury Department said Friday. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: SINGAPORE AUGUST MANUFACTURING OUTPUT UP 8.1% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's manufacturing output grew a less-than-expected 8.1% from a year earlier in August due to a drop in the volatile pharmaceuticals sector. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: VIETNAM SEPTEMBER CPI UP 8.92% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's consumer price index rose 8.92% in September from a year earlier, led by higher prices of housing and building materials, food and education services, the General Statistics Office said Friday. (published 0428 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK OF KOREA TO MAINTAIN SOFT LOAN CEILING AT KRW8.5T IN 4Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea will leave the ceiling on its soft loans to commercial banks unchanged at KRW8.5 trillion in the last quarter of the year, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a statement Friday. (published 0301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: FOOD INFLATION UNLIKELY TO BOOST ASIAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 A spike in food prices may boost overall inflation in Asia, but likely not by enough to seriously accelerate the rise in the region's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0449 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =FOCUS: CHINA SHIFTS PROPERTY MKT FOCUS, TO BOOST CHEAP HOUSING SUPPLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Seeking to stabilize property prices without harming its economy, China is moving toward a strategy of building more public housing rather than tightening the private segment of the market. (published 0452 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO HUNKER DOWN FOR LONGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is in no hurry to raise interest rates. (published 0125 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PETROBRAS RAISES $67 BILLION IN WORLD'S LARGEST SHARE OFFER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazilian government-run oil company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petroleo Brasileiro SA\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or \f28 \uc2 \f2 Petrobras\f28 \uc2 \f2 , late Thursday finalized the terms for the world's largest share offer, setting its sights on turning the Latin American country into one of the world's top oil producers. (published 0407 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par KNOC SHARE OFFER FOR DANA NOW WHOLLY UNCONDITIONAL, CLAIMS 64% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Korea National Oil Corporation\f28 \uc2 \f2 , or KNOC, the state-owned South Korean oil company, Friday declared its offer for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dana Petroleum PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  wholly unconditional and extended it until further notice. (published 0620 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: HYUNDAI ENGINEERING CREDITORS LAUNCH STAKE SALE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Creditors of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Engineering & Construction Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday launched the sale of their 34.88% stake in the construction firm, in a deal that could fetch them $3 billion and potentially set the stage for a fight between \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hyundai Engineering\f28 \uc2 \f2 's former sister companies. (published 0056 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: CABCHARGE FINED A$15M FOR COMPETITION LAW BREACHES, SHARES JUMP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Cabcharge Australia Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . breached Australian competition law and has incurred a A$15 million fine and been ordered to change its practices, the Federal Court in Melbourne ruled Friday. (published 0657 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MARUTI APPOINTS NAKANISHI AS MANAGING DIRECTOR, CEO FOR 3 MORE YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Maruti Suzuki India Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the country's largest car maker by sales, said Friday it has appointed Managing Director and Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shinzo Nakanishi\f28 \uc2 \f2  to the same positions for another three years from Dec. 19. (published 0601 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OVERSEA-CHINESE BANKING CORP: TO MERGE 2 INDONESIAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday said it plans to merge its two licensed bank subsidiaries in Indonesia, PT Bank OCBC Indonesia and PT Bank OCBC NISP. (published 2357 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: OLAM, LOUIS DREYFUS COMMODITIES IN TALKS; MAY LEAD TO MERGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore-listed Olam International Ltd. said Friday it is in preliminary discussions with French group Louis Dreyfus Commodities about a possible business collaboration that may take the form of a merger. (published 0311 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BUMI TO RAISE $360 MLN FROM NONPREEMPTIVE SHARES SALE - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Coal miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 PT Bumi Resources\f28 \uc2 \f2  may raise up to $360 million in net cash from selling 10% of its total equity as shares without preemptive rights, a banker with knowledge of the deal told Dow Jones Newswires on Friday. (published 0244 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =TENAGA EXPECTS UP TO MYR600 MILLION \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  GAINS IN FY2009-10 - CEO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's state-owned power firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tenaga Nasional Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  gains of up to MYR600 million in the fiscal year ended Aug. 31, thanks to the stronger ringgit, Tenaga Chief Executive Che Khalib Mohamad Noh said Friday. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SUNWAY HOLDINGS PLANS $80 MILLION PROPERTY PROJECT IN SRI LANKA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysian builder \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sunway Holdings Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Friday unveiled plans to develop an $80 million property project in Sri Lanka, to become the first Malaysian company to undertake a large-scale property project in the South Asian country. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA TAISAN: TO RAISE UP TO NT$1.56 BLN BY SELLING TDRS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore-registered and listed China Taisan Technology Group Holdings Co. said Friday it plans to raise up to NT$1.56 billion by selling Taiwan Depositary Receipts between Friday and Tuesday. (published 0513 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PUNJAB NATIONAL BANK: DANABANK FOUNDERS MAY NEED TO INFUSE CAPITAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The founders of Kazakhstan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Danabank JSC\f28 \uc2 \f2  may have to infuse capital if needed before India's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Punjab National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  buys a majority stake in it, the Indian lender's executive director said Friday. (published 0542 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NUPLEX: NO DECISION ON POSSIBLE CHANGE IN DOMICILE TO AUSTRALIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nuplex Industries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday it hasn't yet made a decision about changing the company's domicile to Australia. (published 0331 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY LOWER; CHINA SPAT HURTS TOKYO STOCKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bad economic news on the U.S. and European fronts as well as weakness on Wall Street drove most Asian markets lower Friday, with broad-based declines hurting Tokyo and Sydney. (published 0401 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PETROCHINA, HESS IN JOINT EXPLORATION FOR SHALE OIL AT CHINA'S DAQING-SOURCES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PetroChina Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hess Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . have been conducting joint exploration of shale oil resources since early this year at China's flagship Daqing oilfield as part of efforts to shore up output from this aging field, people familiar with the matter said. (published 2158 GMT Thursday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA KEEPS OCTOBER DEADLINE FOR QUEENSLAND LNG DECISIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Australian Environment Minister Tony Burke said Friday that he intends to make a decision on whether to approve two large liquefied natural gas projects in Queensland state by an original October deadline. (published 2312 GMT Thursday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BHP APPROVES US$1.5B WESTERN AUSTRALIA GAS PROJECT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BHP Billiton Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that it has approved the US$1.5 billion development of the Macedon gas field offshore Western Australia state, joining a number of companies wanting to exploit a domestic fuel supply shortage to the state's booming mining sector. (published 2331 GMT Thursday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: RIO TINTO TO SPEND US$230M EXPANDING PORT FOR PILBARA IRON ORE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that it will spend US$230 million expanding iron ore production capacity in the Pilbara region of Western Australia state. (published 0118 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SANTOS AWAITS KOREA GOVERNMENT APPROVAL FOR LNG SALES TO \f28 \uc2 \f2 KOGAS\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Santos Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Chief Executive \f28 \uc2 \f2 David Knox\f28 \uc2 \f2  has told reporters that the company's liquefied natural gas joint venture in Queensland state is awaiting Korean government approval to sell LNG to state-backed \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Gas Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., a Santos spokesman confirmed Friday. (published 2357 GMT Thursday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: IGC CUTS GLOBAL 2010-11 RICE OUTPUT FORECAST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 24-09-10 0710GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The International Grains Council said Friday it has cut its global rice production forecast for 2010-11 by 1.9 million tons to 453.7 million metric tons due to lower-than-expected production in Indonesia and China. (published 0552 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW:AUSTRALIAN RICE OUTPUT TO QUADRUPLE IN 2010-11 - GROWER LOBBY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian rice production could quadruple to 800,000 metric tons in the 2010-11 crop year amid favorable seasonal conditions, paving the way for the resumption of exports in a major way, Executive Director of the Ricegrowers Association of Australia, Ruth Wade, said Friday. (published 0458 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CME ASIA TRADING VOLUMES UP MORE THAN 100% ON YEAR -EXEC \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CME Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . trading volume in Asia is up more than 100% from this time last year, a company executive said Friday. (published 0453 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CME: NO PLANS FOR MORE COMEX GOLD DELIVERY POINTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 CME Group Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has no plans for new delivery points for its benchmark Comex gold futures contracts, CME Executive Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Terry Duffy\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday. (published 0532 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: AUSTRALIA'S BROCKMAN TO UNVEIL A$1.3B IRON ORE MINE FEASIBILITY RESULTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brockman Resources Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that it expects to unveil positive feasibility results next week for its A$1.3 billion Marillana iron ore project in Western Australia's Pilbara region. (published 0539 GMT) [ 24-09-10 0710GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100924e69o000fg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
