ncy\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market if necessary, reminding market participants that Tokyo may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  again to weaken the yen should they push it up too much too quickly. (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: FRENCH 2Q FINAL GDP BETTER THAN INITIAL ESTIMATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The French economy grew faster than initially estimated in the second quarter, supported by consumer spending and gross fixed capital formation, according to official data released Friday. (published 0538 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN PM KAN SUGGESTS FINANCING EXTRA BUDGET WITHOUT BOND ISSUANCE -KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan suggested that the government would not issue any new bonds to finance an extra budget for the current fiscal year, which could include emergency outlays for additional stimulus measures, Kyodo News reported Friday. (published 0139 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: AUSTRALIA POSTS NARROWER DEFICIT, PLEDGES FISCAL DISCIPLINE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Labor government on Friday renewed its commitment to strict fiscal discipline to restore the budget to surplus by the year starting July 1, 2012, after unveiling a narrower-than-expected deficit for the last financial year. (published 0133 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S TREASURY: EXPECTS ECONOMY TO RETURN TO FULL CAPACITY; INFLATION RISK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's economy is expected to reach full capacity in the year ahead with a strong income boost from soaring terms of trade likely to pose inflation risks, Australia's Treasury Department said Friday in a second term briefing note for the recently elected minority Labor government. (published 0523 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: SINGAPORE AUGUST MANUFACTURING OUTPUT UP 8.1% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's manufacturing output grew a less-than-expected 8.1% from a year earlier in August due to a drop in the volatile pharmaceuticals sector. (published 0500 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =DATA SNAP: VIETNAM SEPTEMBER CPI UP 8.92% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vietnam's consumer price index rose 8.92% in September from a year earlier, led by higher prices of housing and building materials, food and education services, the General Statistics Office said Friday. (published 0428 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK OF KOREA TO MAINTAIN SOFT LOAN CEILING AT KRW8.5T IN 4Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Korea will leave the ceiling on its soft loans to commercial banks unchanged at KRW8.5 trillion in the last quarter of the year, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said in a statement Friday. (published 0301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: FOOD INFLATION UNLIKELY TO BOOST ASIAN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 A spike in food prices may boost overall inflation in Asia, but likely not by enough to seriously accelerate the rise in the region's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0449 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =FOCUS: CHINA SHIFTS PROPERTY MKT FOCUS, TO BOOST CHEAP HOUSING SUPPLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Seeking to stabilize property prices without harming its economy, China is moving toward a strategy of building more public housing rather than tightening the private segment of the market. (published 0452 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =FOCUS: CANADAIAN BANKS TO TEST COVERED BONDS DOWN UNDER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Canadian covered-bond issuers are testing a new route to Asia -- through Australia -- that could provide an opening for the covered-bond market to expand beyond its core base in Europe. (published 0556 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =MONEY TALKS: PHILIPPINE \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  TO HUNKER DOWN FOR LONGER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippine \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is in no hurry to raise interest rates. (published 0125 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VIEW: YEN GAINS PROMPT WATCH FOR SIGNS OF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell Thursday to its lowest level in more than a week versus the yen, leaving traders on watch for signs of fresh Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 2024 GMT) [ 24-09-10 0600GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100924e69o000af\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
